# Tests

Test behavior, not private methods. Arrange, act, assert. One purpose per test.

- Policy, severity mapping, and context building use real functions, not mocks.
- Unit tests stay in-process. No network, database, or clock beyond an injected timestamp.
- HTTP tests use Fastify `inject`.
- CI asserts policy outcomes against recorded decision fixtures. A live Jev call is optional and must not be required for the suite to pass.
- Reuse fixtures in `tests/fixtures/`. Do not paste large incident objects into tests.
- Coverage floors are enforced by the test command: 90% domain, 90% policy, 85% application. Do not add tests that only execute lines.

The full standard is `.cursor/harness/testing.md`. A feature is unfinished while its tests fail.
